,"user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2020-11-26T08:45:52Z","updated_at":"2020-12-22T16:53:18Z","closed_at":"2020-12-22T16:53:18Z","author_association":"MEMBER","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nIn https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11421 a user was confused by the fact that `--experimental_enable_runfiles` still exists (undocumented) when `--enable_runfiles` also exists. They thought that these are two different flags, the experimental one maybe being a newer or different implementation.\r\n\r\nIn fact, they're the same flag, but `--experimental_enable_runfiles` was the `oldName` of the flag: https://cs.opensource.google/bazel/bazel/+/8eae6b34ec6e1e83010b17094d1225f045606eb2:src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/analysis/config/CoreOptions.java;l=722\r\n\r\n### Feature requests: what underlying problem are you trying to solve with this feature?\r\n\r\nWe should print a warning if a flag is passed by its `oldName` to Bazel that tells the user that the name is deprecated and might go away in the future. The warning should also contain the new name of the flag.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/subscriptions"